      "dom_id": "question-19951",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "There are $11$ people taking an online quiz at the same time. How many ways can people finish in first, second, and third place, assuming there are no ties?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $11$ people, so $n=11.$ We want to select $3$ of those people to come first, second, or third, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to place the people is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{11}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{11!}{(11-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11!}{8!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot \\cancel{8!}}{\\cancel{8!}} \\\\  & =11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =990.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
