      "dom_id": "question-84981",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The $8$ members of a club are asked to elect $4$ officials: a president, a vice-president, a secretary, and a treasurer. How many different ways of electing the officials are possible?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $8$ members to choose from, so $n=8.$ We want to select $4$ of those members to be officials, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different $4$-member official teams is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{8}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{8!}{(8-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8!}{4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1\\,680.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
