      "dom_id": "question-122483",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Erika has a crayon box with $36$ different colors. She wants to draw each side of a square with a different color. How many possible choices of colors does Erika have?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $36$ colors to choose from, so $n=36.$ We want to select $4$ of those colors to draw the sides of the square, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of possible choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{36}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{36!}{(36-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{36!}{32!} \\\\  & =\\frac{36\\cdot 35\\cdot 34\\cdot 33\\cdot \\cancel{32!}}{\\cancel{32!}} \\\\  & =36\\cdot 35\\cdot 34\\cdot 33 \\\\  & =1\\,413\\,720.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
